    "notes": [
      "The figure: 7-28 V in, 3.3 V / 3 A out. VOUT = 0.8 V x (1 + R5 / R6); R5 about 10 kohm.",
      "Compensation: R3 in series with C6 from COMP to ground, C7 from COMP to ground in parallel (COMP_RC is the node between R3 and C6).",
      "The catch diode carries the inductor current while the switch is off: a 40 V 3 A Schottky for inputs up to 28 V."
    ],
    "page": "p. 14, Figure 8-1 (7-28 V in, 3.3 V / 3 A out)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Keep the loop VIN capacitors, PH, catch diode and GND short; VSENSE and COMP away from the PH node.",
    "EN floats high (enabled); the R1/R2 divider sets the start voltage (about 6.5 V here)."
  ],
